<title>HUNGARY: OTP releases Jan-June IAS results.</title>
<headline>OTP releases Jan-June IAS results.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					   Jan-June 96    Jan-Dec 95</p>
<p>Group income before income</p>
<p>     taxes and minority interest    6,298    vs    9,635</p>
<p>Group income after income</p>
<p>taxes and before minority</p>
<p>     interest			     4,617    vs    7,499</p>
<p>    Group net income		    4,656    vs    7,495</p>
<p>    Group net interest income	28,841    vs   52,943</p>
<p>     Group interest income	   96,582    vs  181,386</p>
<p>     Group interest expense	  67,741    vs  128,443</p>
<p>Group provision for possible</p>
<p>     loan losses			  3,632    vs    9,260</p>
<p>Group net interest income after</p>
<p>loan provision for possible</p>
<p>     loan losses			 25,209    vs   43,683</p>
<p>    Group non-interest income	14,539    vs   28,460</p>
<p>    Group non-interest expense     33,450    vs   64,206</p>
<p>    Group income taxes		  1,681    vs    2,136</p>
<p>    Minority interest		  39 profit vs    4 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Orszagos Takarekpenztar es Kereskedelmi Bank Rt is Hungary's largest commercial bank. The figures are consolidated and are calculated according to International Accounting Standards (IAS). They are not audited.</p>
<p>OTP Bank has prepared its consolidated IAS report for the first half of 1996. Since there is no available report on the first half of 1995, the report includes data for the whole year of 1995 as comparison.</p>
<p>OTP released its first half results, which were calculated according to Hungarian Accounting Stardards, on August 15.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
